<resources>
    <!-- Default screen margins, per the Android Design guidelines. -->
    <dimen name="activity_horizontal_margin">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="activity_vertical_margin">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="fab_margin">16dp</dimen>

    <!-- UI Text Size -->
    <dimen name="textsize_connection">20dp</dimen>

    <!-- List View Relative -->
    <dimen name="item_arrow_width">26dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_arrow_height">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_min_height">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_value_size">18sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_title_size">18sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="test_log_textsize">17sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="button_widget">200dp</dimen>
    <!-- Flight-screen mini-map edge. The HUD's right-hand column is the tightest space in the
         app: toolbar, exposure block, telemetry and map all share one landscape screen height,
         and the map is the single largest item. This default is sized for SHORT screens (a
         Samsung S21 is ~411dp tall in landscape); values-h440dp gives taller devices the bigger
         map. Shrinking the map rather than the text keeps the readout legible in daylight,
         which is the part that actually has to work in the field. -->
    <!-- ⚠ REDUCED to pay for the HUD panels. The two panels add
         4dp of padding at the top and bottom of each, 16dp in total, and this bucket had only
         5dp of slack in the worst case (FAA ceiling visible). Worst case is now:

             paddingTop 60 + EV slider 24 + map 110 + paddingBottom 12 + margins 20
               + 16 x 10 text lines + 2 panels x 8dp padding = 402dp

         ⚠ paddingTop is 8dp now (the actions left the band, the EV slider rose
         to the band's top), so every figure below has 52dp more slack than it says. Measured
         on the RC Plus 2: root 480dp, map bottom 477dp.

         against 411dp of screen, so 9dp of slack. The remedy is to take the height from
         flight_map_size, never by re-joining
         the readout lines. **This is arithmetic, not a measurement.**

         ⚠ RE-COUNTED FOR THE HUD REFRESH, AND IT CAME OUT LEVEL:

             - 2 panels x 8dp of vertical padding      -16dp   (the panels are gone)
             + 7 outlined views x about 1.6dp          +11dp   (OutlinedTextView's own padding)
             + the height size hierarchy               + 4dp   (net of the smaller unit
                                                                and position line)
                                                       =======
                                                       -1dp

         The panels were paying for the outline and did not know it. The vertical 4dp they
         supplied is DELIBERATELY NOT restored on the blocks — see the flight layout — because
         that is the 16dp above, and without it this refresh would not fit on this device.

         ⚠ THIS IS STILL ARITHMETIC AND STILL NOT A MEASUREMENT, and it is now a tighter piece
         of arithmetic than before. MEASURE IT with `dumpsys activity top` on the RC Plus 2
         before a release. The failure mode is the mini-map clipped SILENTLY at the
         bottom of the column. Adding ONE more outlined readout costs about 1.6dp. -->
    <!-- ⚠ 148dp, NOT 110dp. This is the COLUMN width, thus it is also the
         width the aircraft's latitude and longitude have to print in. At 110dp the pair wrapped
         onto two lines on the RC Plus 2. The coordinate line is about 18 characters
         at roughly 6dp each, about 108dp, and the panel adds 8dp of padding on each side — so
         the column needs about 124dp before the pair fits on one line, and 148dp leaves room
         for a third digit of longitude.

         Raising this widens the MAP too, because the map takes the column's width. That is
         accepted here: the RC Plus 2 is 768dp wide and the column costs 152dp of it.
         flight_map_height is deliberately NOT raised with it — the vertical budget above has
         only about 14dp of slack on this device, while width is abundant. -->
    <!-- WARNING BANNER, per device. What the banner IS — white bold, severity on the
         background — is fixed; these two numbers belong to the device.
         At 15sp in 380dp the banner covered about a third of the RC Plus
         2's video, because this screen is only 768dp wide.
         13sp fits the same text in fewer, shorter lines. The width stays 380dp:
         narrowing it does not shrink the banner, it makes it TALLER, and height is what
         covers the picture. -->
    <!-- ⚠ RE-SIZED BY PROPORTION: these were
         a 1024x720dp controller's 15sp/480dp scaled only by eye, and on this panel — where a dp
         is 24 % larger than nominal — the banner still read as full size.
         Scaled the way the column pills were: 15sp by the screens' height ratio
         (480/720) is 10sp; 11sp is the floor the outline and bold still read at. The width
         follows the text (11/13 of 380 is 320) so the LINE COUNT does not grow — narrowing
         the box without shrinking the text makes the banner taller, and height is what
         covers the picture. The ✕ is the column's control height, one target size across the
         screen. Paddings 8/6/4/4 from 12/8/6/6, the same two-thirds. -->
    <dimen name="flight_warning_text_size">11sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_warning_max_width">320dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_warning_padding_start">8dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_warning_padding_end">6dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_warning_padding_v">4dp</dimen>
    <!-- The banner's ✕ close button. A touch target, not a glyph box: the same 30dp as every
         control in the band and the column on this controller; the ✕ it holds is about 8dp
         wide. It ADDS to the banner width, thus max_width above no longer bounds the whole
         banner. -->
    <dimen name="flight_warning_close_size">@dimen/hud_column_pill_height</dimen>
    <!-- The transient notice (top-centre): the same 11sp as the banner, by the same
         proportion, and hung 8dp under the 44dp band (it was 64dp under the top, set when
         the band was 60). -->
    <dimen name="flight_notice_text_size">11sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_notice_margin_top">52dp</dimen>
    <!-- THE ANTENNA-AIM ARC'S PLACE. It was bottom-centre
         (x 344-428dp) and the banner, now bottom-left, ran under it: x 80 to as far
         as 430 (flight_left_chrome_clear 80 + max width 320 + the 30dp close). The arc goes
         into the strip the banner can never reach, between the banner's furthest right edge
         and the HUD column:

             strip   = 80 + 320 + 30 + 8 air = 438  ..  602 (the HUD column's left)
             arc     = (40dp radius + 3 x 5dp marker) x 2 = 110dp wide (AntennaAimView)
             centre  = (438 + 602) / 2 = 520   →   start = 520 - 55 = 465dp

         Move the banner's width or the HUD column and this moves with them. -->
    <dimen name="flight_antenna_arc_margin_start">465dp</dimen>

    <!-- The accessory panel (L2). 280dp of a 768dp screen — wide enough for a usable brightness
         slider, and it still leaves the crosshair and the whole right-hand HUD column clear.
         Do not grow it past a third of the width: it opens over live video in flight. -->
    <dimen name="accessory_panel_width">280dp</dimen>

    <dimen name="flight_map_size">148dp</dimen>
    <!-- ⚠ DERIVED, NOT A FREE NUMBER: flight_map_size + the HUD column's paddingEnd, which is
         4dp (it was 14dp, which left a visible gap against the right edge of
         the screen). 148 + 4 = 152. Change this in EVERY bucket whenever either input moves;
         it is a MUST because it has silently broken twice. -->
    <dimen name="flight_resource_row_margin_end">152dp</dimen>
    <!-- Separate from flight_map_size so a taller screen can carry a taller map
         without a wider HUD column. Equal to the width today, so the map is square
         and nothing moved when this was introduced. -->
    <!-- ⚠ 119dp, AND THE COLUMN'S paddingBottom CAME DOWN 12->3 TO PAY FOR IT.
         The corner now carries the vision-assist view as well as the map, and its bottom edge
         lines up with the L3 "IR" chip on the opposite side of the screen (design decision).
         That chip's stack sits 3dp off the bottom, so the column's bottom padding had to match —
         and the 9dp that freed went straight into the map, which is why the VERTICAL BUDGET
         ABOVE IS UNCHANGED at about 402dp. ⚠ Do not raise this without taking the height from
         somewhere; overflow clips the map with no warning and no log line. -->
    <dimen name="flight_map_height">119dp</dimen>
    <!-- HUD readout size, per bucket. 12sp is what hudText already used, so this
         changed no pixel; it exists so a controller can raise it.
         On a sunlight-readable screen at arm's length 12sp is too small. -->
    <dimen name="flight_readout_text_size">12sp</dimen>

    <!-- HUD CHROME DIMENSIONS.

         ⚠ THE BASE BUCKET IS THE RC PLUS 2's BUCKET. This build has one target and no phone to
         share with, so these ARE its per-device values; this controller draws readouts at
         12sp. -->

    <!-- The one edge weight the whole HUD shares — readouts, EV slider, map frame. About an
         EIGHTH of the readout text size, which is 12sp here.
         ⚠ TOO WIDE AND THE READOUTS TURN TO BLACK BLOBS: the stroke is CENTRED on the glyph
         edge, so half of it falls inside the letter and is covered by the fill. -->
    <dimen name="hud_text_outline_width">1.5dp</dimen>

    <!-- The shape of every toggle pill: AR, zoom, re-sync, LIVE, REC, and the mini-map's zoom
         button. The mini-map's corners take hud_pill_radius too.
         ⚠ 8dp IS NOT hud_control_radius. The capsule is the container and takes the large
         radius; the pills INSIDE it take the small one, and so does the map, which is read
         rather than pressed. -->
    <dimen name="hud_pill_radius">8dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="hud_pill_stroke">1.5dp</dimen>

    <!-- The floating toolbar capsules. Large radius: "you touch this". -->
    <dimen name="hud_control_radius">20dp</dimen>

    <!-- ⚠ BOTH TOOLBAR CAPSULES MUST BE THIS TALL, AND IT IS A MINIMUM, NOT A HEIGHT.
         The two clusters hold different things, so they measure differently: the ACTIONS
         capsule's tallest child is the 46dp drop pin and the STATUS capsule's is a 34dp icon.
         Two capsules that begin on the same line and end on different ones read as a mistake.

         ⚠ IT IS DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN: the actions capsule's natural height, which is the drop
         pin plus the capsule's own paddingVertical on each side.

             46dp drop pin + 2 x 3dp paddingVertical = 52dp

         A value BELOW that does nothing at all === the actions capsule is already taller, and
         the status capsule stays short. It was 40dp once, and the capsules were not level.
         If the drop pin or the padding changes, this changes with them.

         A MINIMUM rather than a fixed height because either cluster may still grow: a longer
         signal readout, a taller button style, a density not yet seen. minHeight can only make
         a capsule taller, thus it can never clip its own content. -->
    <!-- ⚠ RE-DERIVED. The actions left the band for the column,
         taking the 46dp drop pin with them; the band's controls then took the column's pill
         height, so the capsule's tallest child
         is a 30dp control:

             30dp control + 2 x 3dp paddingVertical = 36dp

         and the band is 8dp paddingTop + 36dp = 44dp. The band's height is the top chrome
         inset for the AR overlay and the obstacle view, and hud_column_margin_top derives
         from it — move this and move that. -->
    <dimen name="hud_capsule_height">36dp</dimen>

    <!-- ===== THE ACTIONS COLUMN (measured) =====
         The seven action pills stand in ONE vertical column at the top-left of the video.
         Every number below was measured on the RC Plus 2 with
         `dumpsys activity top`; no dp value transfers between devices.

         THE SCREEN: the flight activity hides the status bar (48dp) and the navigation bar
         (16dp) and lays out under both, so the root FrameLayout is 768 x 480dp — not the
         416dp `am get-config` reports, nor the 464dp the hardware doc assumed. Measured as
         `android:id/content 0,0-1920,1200` at 2.5 px/dp, with both bar backgrounds 0px tall.

         THE BUDGET (seven pills; no PIP, no thermal-size pill on MSDKv5):

             7 x 30dp pills               210dp
             6 x 10dp gaps                 60dp
             2 x  8dp paddingVertical      16dp
                                          ======
             column                       286dp
             + marginTop                   48dp   (band 44 + 4)
                                          ======
                                          334dp   of 480dp, 146dp clear above the bottom edge.

         ⚠ SIZED BY PROPORTION, NOT BY COPYING. The first cut kept a 42dp pill height taken
         from a 1024x720dp controller; measured on the device it put
         the column at y 64-450 and it was plainly too large for this panel, and it buried the
         L1/L2 hint chips at the bottom-left (MARK at y 383, ACC at 421). A 42dp pill
         is 5.8 % of a 720dp screen height; 42dp here is 8.75 % of 480. Scaling that
         column by the two screens' heights (480/720 = 2/3) gives 28dp pills and a 12dp gap,
         and by their widths (768/1024 = 3/4) a 50dp pill; rounded to what the labels need,
         that is 52 x 30 with a 10dp gap. The column's foot at 334dp clears the chips by 49dp.

         A dp on this panel is about 24 % larger than nominal, so a 30dp pill here is a
         touch target of about the physical size of a 37dp one at nominal density. -->

    <!-- ONE width and ONE height for all seven. 52dp holds "▶ LIVE" and "● REC" at 13sp
         (the toggle views measure their own text; see them) and the four-glyph "2.4X" the
         zoom pill can show. 30dp is the proportional height — see the budget above. -->
    <dimen name="hud_column_pill_width">52dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="hud_column_pill_height">30dp</dimen>
    <!-- The gap between pills: a third of a pill (the 18-of-42 ratio the column was scaled from). -->
    <dimen name="hud_column_pill_gap">10dp</dimen>
    <!-- The capsule's own padding. 6dp sideways: the column is 52 + 12 + 8 margin = 72dp of a
         768dp screen, and the banner and the left obstacle label start to its right. 8dp
         vertically: the capsule corners (hud_control_radius, 20dp) eat into the first and
         last pill, so they get a little more air than the sides. -->
    <dimen name="hud_column_padding_h">6dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="hud_column_padding_v">8dp</dimen>
    <!-- The label size on the text pills (AR, IR, zoom). 13sp: the band's pills were 14sp
         in a 34dp box; a 30dp box takes one step down and the glyphs still clear the stroke. -->
    <dimen name="hud_column_pill_text">13sp</dimen>
    <!-- Below the band. The band measures 44dp (8dp paddingTop + the 36dp status capsule);
         4dp of air under it. The band's
         height is the AR overlay's top chrome inset, thus this margin and that inset agree. -->
    <dimen name="hud_column_margin_top">48dp</dimen>
    <!-- Flush with the band's own 8dp paddingHorizontal, so the column's left edge and the
         status capsule's left edge are one line. -->
    <dimen name="hud_column_margin_start">8dp</dimen>

    <!-- WHAT STARTS TO THE RIGHT OF THE COLUMN. The column's right edge
         is marginStart 8 + paddingHorizontal 6 + pill 52 + 6 = 72dp, measured as 72 on the
         RC Plus 2. 8dp of air, the column's own margin, puts these at 80dp. The
         warning banner starts to the right of the column — on THIS screen the two were expected
         to overlap in Y, and they do not (the column's foot is 334dp, the banner's
         top about 440), but the L1/L2/L3 hint chips DO stand at the bottom-left, 58dp wide
         (MARK at y 383-402), so the banner needs the same clearance for them. One number,
         derived once, for everything that must not sit on the column. -->
    <dimen name="flight_left_chrome_clear">80dp</dimen>

    <!-- THE EMERGENCY BROADCAST NOTICE. PER-DEVICE, exactly like the warning
         banner's size: the notice sits at the TOP in the gap between the status capsule and the
         EV slider, anchored to the start of that gap and vertically centred on the capsule.

         ⚠ **MEASURED ON THE RC Plus 2, NOT COMPUTED** — and the computed version of
         these numbers was wrong in a way that would have shipped. Read off a screenshot of the
         flight screen with the notice forced visible, at 1920x1200 px and 400 dpi, so 1dp =
         2.5px on this panel:
           status capsule          x 20-768 px   =   8 - 307dp   (so its right edge is 307dp,
                                                                  not the 315dp the child widths
                                                                  predicted)
           EV slider "-2" label    x 1563 px     = 625dp         (the real obstacle — the label
                                                                  stands further left than the
                                                                  slider line at 1581 px / 632dp)
           the notice at 11sp      800 px wide   = 320dp         of a 318dp gap
         So 11sp DID NOT FIT: the notice ran 35dp under the EV label, over a live control. The
         per-device lever is the text size, so the notice runs at 10sp here. VERIFIED
         at 10sp on the same device: the capsule measures x 790-1505 px = 316-602dp, 286dp wide,
         clearing the EV label by 23dp. The WORDING is fixed and is not to be shortened.

         marginStart = the capsule's measured right edge (307 -> 308) + 8dp of air, the band's
         own rhythm. marginTop centres the notice on the capsule's centre, which the same
         screenshot puts at 65 px = 26dp; VERIFIED at 14dp, which puts the notice's own centre
         at 26.6dp (it was 20dp and sat 7dp low).
         The notice is inside the band's 44dp height, so a tap on it lands on the notice and not
         on the video.

         ⚠ Re-measure all three whenever the status capsule gains or loses a control, or either
         of its two wrap_content text views (the signal "%" and the satellite count) changes
         shape. Nothing here derives itself. -->
    <dimen name="flight_emergency_notice_margin_start">316dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_emergency_notice_margin_top">14dp</dimen>
    <!-- 10sp, below the 11sp notice/banner size used elsewhere on this screen, because
         the measurement above left no other way to keep the specified wording out of the EV
         slider. A dp on this 400dpi panel is about 24 % larger than nominal, so 10sp here is
         about a nominal 12sp. -->
    <dimen name="flight_emergency_notice_text_size">10sp</dimen>

    <!-- THE FLIGHT SCREEN'S TAK CHANNELS DIALOG, scaled down a quarter.
         PER-DEVICE: this dialog opens over live video on a 768dp-wide, 480dp-high screen, and it
         carries TWO channel lists since the Elevated account joined it. Measured on the RC Plus
         2 with six Standard channels: the dialog reached the full height of the screen
         and the Elevated section was CUT OFF below the fold — the pilot could see its heading
         and nothing under it, which is worse than not showing it, because it reads as an empty
         list rather than as more to scroll to.

         ⚠ THE ROW HEIGHT IS NOT CUT BY A QUARTER, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. These rows are touch
         targets over live video, and a miss changes who sees this aircraft. The TEXT comes down
         13sp -> 10sp and 14sp -> 11sp, and the padding with it; the row goes 32dp -> 30dp, which
         is hud_column_pill_height, the established minimum for a control the pilot aims
         at in flight. On this 400dpi panel a dp is about 24 % larger than nominal, so 30dp here
         is about the physical size of a 37dp target elsewhere. Do not take the row below this
         to win another line.

         ⚠ 36dp WAS TRIED FIRST AND MADE IT WORSE. The platform's own default for these rows is
         32dp, so a 36dp "minimum" RAISED them and the dialog grew while the text shrank. Read
         the default off the device before setting a floor. -->
    <dimen name="chan_dialog_text_size">10sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="chan_dialog_row_text_size">11sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="chan_dialog_row_min_height">30dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="chan_dialog_pad">14dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="chan_dialog_gap">6dp</dimen>

</resources>
